  ["creature.sammaster-dracolich-form.fraif2014"]={title="Sammaster (Dracolich Form)",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 275\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 276 (24d12 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Sammaster fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLife Suppression\n\nCreatures within 60 feet of Sammaster can't regain XPHB.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSammaster has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Gem\n\nSammaster has a magical soul gem as his dracolich heart. The gem can't be damaged or removed until he is reduced to 0 XPHB. If Sammaster is reduced to 0 XPHB, his dracolich form dissolves to dust. After 1d10 days, he appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of his soul gem (so long as the gem still exists), using the Sammaster (Lich Form) stat block. The gem is a Tiny object that has AC 20; HP 50; and XPHB to Acid, Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The gem regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSammaster makes three Rend attacks. He can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB (level 6 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 10 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Slashing damage plus 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nCorroding Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 52 (8d12) Acid or Necrotic damage (Sammaster's choice). actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nSammaster moves up to half his XPHB, and he makes one Rend attack.\n\nSickening Ray\n\nSammaster uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 6 version).\n\nTerrifying Presence\n\nwis 21, each creature in a 20-foot XPHB originating from Sammaster. actSaveFail 13 (2d12) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail Sammaster can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["creature.sammaster-lich-form.fraif2014"]={title="Sammaster (Lich Form)",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 322 (43d8 + 129)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Sammaster fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLife Suppression\n\nCreatures within 60 feet of Sammaster can't regain XPHB.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSammaster has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Gem\n\nIf Sammaster is reduced to 0 XPHB while his magical soul gem exists, his lich form dissolves to dust. After 1d10 days, he appears in the space of his soul gem, using the Sammaster (Dracolich Form) stat block. The gem is a Tiny object that has AC 20; HP 50; and XPHB to Acid, Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The gem regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB. If the gem is destroyed, Sammaster can create a new one by completing an 8-hour ritual using a gem worth 1,000+ GP, which the ritual consumes, and by expending 5,000 GP.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSammaster makes three attacks, using Corrosive Burst or Paralyzing Touch in any combination. He can replace two attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nCorrosive Burst\n\nm,r 13, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h38 (5d12 + 6) Acid or Necrotic damage (Sammaster's choice).\n\nParalyzing Touch\n\nm 13, reach 5 ft. h16 (3d6 + 6) Cold damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Sammaster's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeathly Teleport\n\nSammaster teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space he can see, and each creature within 10 feet of the space he left takes 19 (3d12) Necrotic damage.\n\nDissolve\n\nSammaster makes one Corrosive Burst attack.\n\nTerrifying Presence\n\nwis 21, each creature in a 20-foot XPHB originating from Sammaster. actSaveFail 13 (2d12) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail Sammaster can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["subclass.samurai.xge2024.fighter.samurai.0"]={title="Samurai",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nPagina: 31\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Fighting Spirit\n\nPagina: 31\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your intensity in battle can shield you and help you strike true. As a bonus action on your turn, you can give yourself advantage on weapon attack rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain 5 temporary hit points. The number of temporary hit points increases when you reach certain levels in this class, increasing to 10 at 10th level and 15 at 15th level.\n\nYou can use this feature three times, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Samurai\n\nPagina: 31\n\nThe Samurai is a fighter who draws on an implacable fighting spirit to overcome enemies. A Samurai's resolve is nearly unbreakable, and the enemies in a Samurai's path have two choices: yield or die fighting.\n\nNivel 7 - Elegant Courtier\n\nPagina: 31\n\nStarting at 7th level, your discipline and attention to detail allow you to excel in social situations. Whenever you make a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier.\n\nYour self-control also causes you to gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have this proficiency, you instead gain proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws (your choice).\n\nNivel 7 - Elegant Courtier\n\nNivel 10 - Tireless Spirit\n\nPagina: 31\n\nStarting at 10th level, when you roll initiative and have no uses of Fighting Spirit remaining, you regain one use.\n\nNivel 15 - Rapid Strike\n\nPagina: 31\n\nStarting at 15th level, you learn to trade accuracy for swift strikes. If you take the Attack action on your turn and have advantage on an attack roll against one of the targets, you can forgo the advantage for that roll to make an additional weapon attack against that target, as part of the same action. You can do so no more than once per turn.\n\nNivel 18 - Strength before Death\n\nPagina: 31\n\nStarting at 18th level, your fighting spirit can delay the grasp of death. If you take damage that reduces you to 0 hit points and doesn't kill you outright, you can use your reaction to delay falling unconscious, and you can immediately take an extra turn, interrupting the current turn. While you have 0 hit points during that extra turn, taking damage causes death saving throw failures as normal, and three death saving throw failures can still kill you. When the extra turn ends, you fall unconscious if you still have 0 hit points.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.samurai.xge2024.fighter.samurai.3"]={title="Samurai",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 31\n\nThe Samurai is a fighter who draws on an implacable fighting spirit to overcome enemies. A Samurai's resolve is nearly unbreakable, and the enemies in a Samurai's path have two choices: yield or die fighting."},
  ["creature.sanbalet.gos2014"]={title="Sanbalet",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 252\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.sanctuary.phb2014"]={title="Sanctuary",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nYou ward a creature within range against attack. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack or a harmful spell must first make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature must choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn't protect the warded creature from area effects, such as the explosion of a fireball.\n\nIf the warded creature makes an attack, casts a spell that affects an enemy, or deals damage to another creature, this spell ends."},
  ["spell.sanctuary.xphb2024"]={title="Sanctuary",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nYou ward a creature within range. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack roll or a damaging spell must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or either choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn't protect the warded creature from areas of effect.\n\nThe spell ends if the warded creature makes an attack roll, casts a spell, or deals damage."},
  ["reward.sanctuary-charm.xdmg2024"]={title="Sanctuary Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 345\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your XDMG, you gain a magical Charm (see \"XDMG\" in XDMG) that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot. You can't gain this Charm again while you still have it."},
  ["feature.sanctuary-vessel.tce2014.warlock.genie.10"]={title="Sanctuary Vessel",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.sanctum-amulet.bgg2014"]={title="Sanctum Amulet",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nA black opal pendant hangs at the base of this pearlescent chain. The sacred rune is inscribed on the back of the pendant.\n\nWhile wearing this item, you have resistance to necrotic damage. Additionally, you can cast the spare the dying cantrip using either an action or a bonus action.\n\nInvoking the Rune\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 60 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points as a result of taking damage, you can use your reaction to invoke the item's rune, causing the pendant to flash with pale light. The creature then instead drops to 1 hit point.\n\nOnce the rune has been invoked, it can't be invoked again until the next dawn."},
  ["reward.sanctum-charm.xdmg2024"]={title="Sanctum Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 346\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your XDMG, you gain a magical Charm (see \"XDMG\" in XDMG) that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot. You can't gain this Charm again while you still have it."},
  ["creature.sandesyl-morgia.hotdq2014"]={title="Sandesyl Morgia",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sandwurm.psa2014"]={title="Sandwurm",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sangora.veor2014"]={title="Sangora",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sangzor.cos2014"]={title="Sangzor",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 1\n\nPV: 33 (3d10 + 3)\n\nINT 6\n\nResistencias:"},
  ["magicitem.sapphire-buckler.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Buckler",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis crystalline blue shield is fashioned from a sapphire dragon's scale and is created to aid in rooting out the influence of Aberrations. While wielding the shield, you have resistance to psychic and thunder damage. Also, when you take damage from a creature that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to deal 2d6 thunder damage to that creature.\n\nAs an action, you can use the shield to help you locate Aberrations until the end of your next turn. If any Aberrations are within 1 mile of you, the shield emits a low humming tone for a moment, and you know the direction of all Aberrations within that range. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.sapphire-dragon-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, climb: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 5-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) thunder damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated."},
  ["creature.sapphire-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 24 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGem Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 400 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use its Mass Telekinesis action during the next hour. Award a party an additional 90,000 XP (180,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Gem Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales crushing force in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 71 (11d12) force damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. On a success or failure, the creature's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\nMass Telekinesis (Gem Awakening Only; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe greatwyrm targets any number of creatures and objects it can see within 120 feet of it. No one target can weigh more than 4,000 pounds, and objects can't be targeted if they're being worn or carried. Each targeted creature must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be restrained in the greatwyrm's telekinetic grip. At the end of a creature's turn, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nAt the end of the greatwyrm's turn, it can move each creature or object it has in its telekinetic grip up to 60 feet in any direction, but not beyond 120 feet of itself. In addition, it can choose any number of creatures restrained in this way and deal 45 (7d12) force damage to each of them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the greatwyrm is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe greatwyrm magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nPsychic Beam (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm emits a beam of psychic energy in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Intelligence saving throw, taking 27 (5d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.sapphire-sentinel.cm2014"]={title="Sapphire Sentinel",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe golem's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nSlow {@recharge 5}\n\nThe golem targets one or more creatures it can see within 10 feet of it. Each target must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw against this magic. On a failed save, a target can't use reactions, its speed is halved, and it can't make more than one attack on its turn. In addition, the target can take either an action or a bonus action on its turn, not both. These effects last for 1 minute. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nSapphire\n\nThe sapphire has 3 charges. As an action, the golem can expend 1 charge to cast dispel magic (as a 9th-level spell) from the sapphire using Constitution as its spellcasting ability. The sapphire ceases to glow if all its charges are expended, but it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn and glows again once it has 1 or more charges."},
  ["spell.sapping-sting.egw2014"]={title="Sapping Sting",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\nYou sap the vitality of one creature you can see in range. The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d4 necrotic damage and fall prone.\n\nThis spell's damage increases by 1d4 when you reach 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4), and 17th level (4d4)."},
  ["creature.sarcelle-malinosh.veor2014"]={title="Sarcelle Malinosh",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.sardonyx.dmg2014"]={title="Sardonyx",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque bands of red and white gemstone."},
  ["item.sardonyx.xdmg2024"]={title="Sardonyx",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA bands of red and white gemstone."},
  ["creature.sarevok.coa2014"]={title="Sarevok",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 190 (20d8 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 11 | WIS 18 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSarevok has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Sarevok is killed, he gains a new body in 24 hours, regaining all his hit points. The new body appears on the altar of the temple of Bhaal beneath Baldur's Gate. This ability ceases to function if a cleric of good alignment casts Hallow on the altar in the temple of Bhaal.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSarevok makes three Longsword attacks. He can replace one of the attacks with Flames of Bhaal or Spellcasting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage or 11 (1d10 + 6) if wielded in two hands. The target must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or be cursed by Bhaal, preventing it from regaining hit points. The curse lasts until removed by the Remove Curse spell or similar effect.\n\nFlames of Bhaal\n\nSarevok causes flames to engulf one creature that he can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a 18 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) necrotic damage. This damage can't be restored except by a Lesser Restoration spell or similar effect.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nSlash\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack.\n\nUnholy Flame\n\nSarevok uses Flames of Bhaal.\n\nChannel Bhaal's Hate (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSarevok unleashes Bhaal's power. Creatures within 30 feet of Sarevok, including ones behind barriers and around corners, can't regain hit points until the end of Sarevok's next turn."},
  ["creature.sarevok.mabjov2014"]={title="Sarevok",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 153 (18d8 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSarevok has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Sarevok is killed he gains a new body in 24 hours, regaining all his hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears on the altar of the temple of Bhaal beneath Baldur's Gate. This ability ceases to function if a cleric of good alignment casts Hallow on the altar in the temple of Bhaal.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSarevok makes two Longsword attacks. He may replace one of the attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage or 10 (1d10 + 5) if wielded in two hands. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be cursed by Bhaal. The cursed target can't regain hit points. The curse lasts until removed by the remove curse spell or other magic.\n\nAssassin's Strike\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack. If he hits the target and has advantage on the attack roll, then he deals an additional 21 (6d6) poison damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or have the poisoned condition for 10 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack.\n\nUnholy Flame\n\nSarevok casts sacred flame.\n\nChannel Bhaal's Hate (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSarevok unleashes Bhaal's power. Creatures within 30 feet of Sarevok, including ones behind barriers and around corners, can't regain hit points until the end of Sarevok's next turn."},
  ["deity.sargonnas.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sargonnas",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nSargonnas is the unpredictable god of flame, vengeance, and wrath. Though he's a consort to Takhisis, he schemes against her as often as he fights on her behalf. He is worshiped by those who seek retribution. His true form is that of a monstrous minotaur, and many minotaurs revere him under the name Sargas."},
  ["deity.sargonnas.phb2014"]={title="Sargonnas",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["creature.sarith-kzekarit.oota2014"]={title="Sarith Kzekarit",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sarlamir.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sarlamir",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.sarlona-trinket.erlw2014"]={title="Sarlona Trinket",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd8 | Trinket\n\n1 | A polished crystal sphere; when you clutch it in your fist, a telepathic voice recites a story in your mind\n\n2 | A teardrop pendant made from polished shell; when you hold it, you see the image of a young Riedran man\n\n3 | A six-sided crystal die; when you roll it, you feel a surge of emotion for six seconds\n\n4 | A sealed vial filled with faintly luminescent blue mist\n\n5 | A crystal disk engraved with a labyrinthine pattern\n\n6 | A leather-bound collection of kalashtar poetry called Shards of the Light\n\n7 | A sphere of polished crystal; when you hold it in your palm, you feel that it knows you and understands you\n\n8 | A cup and ball toy; when you successfully catch the ball in the cup, you feel a momentary surge of joy"},
  ["creature.sarrukh-tyrant.aud2014"]={title="Sarrukh Tyrant",subtitle="Criatura - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 256 (27d8 + 135)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 23 | WIS 19 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the sarrukh fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe sarrukh has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sarrukh makes two attacks, using Bite or Fearsome Fauchard in any combination.\n\nBite\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d6 + 6) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Poison damage.\n\nFearsome Fauchard\n\nm,r 12, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it has the XPHB condition. If the target already has the XPHB condition, it takes an additional 10 (3d6) Psychic damage. homThe fauchard magically returns to the sarrukh's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShape Control\n\nactTrigger A creature the sarrukh can see shape-shifts. actResponse The sarrukh chooses the resulting form from among the options available to the shape-shifting creature or prevents the creature from shape-shifting.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFearsome Glance\n\nwis 20, one creature the sarrukh can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\nSlither\n\nThe sarrukh moves up to half its XPHB without provoking XPHB, and it makes one Bite attack.\n\nTwisted Transformation\n\nThe sarrukh uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB, and if the target fails its saving throw, the target also has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. The sarrukh can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["deity.sarula-iliene.mtf2014"]={title="Sarula Iliene",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.sarusanda-allester.veor2014"]={title="Sarusanda Allester",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Elvish, any four languages, telepathy 120 ft."},
  ["creature.satyr.mm2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 31 (7d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["species.satyr.mot2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Especie - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nAge\n\nSatyrs mature and age at about the same rate as humans.\n\nAlignment\n\nSatyrs delight in living a life free of the mantle of law. They gravitate toward being good, but some have devious streaks and enjoy causing dismay.\n\nSize\n\nSatyrs range from just under 5 feet to about 6 feet in height, with generally slender builds. Your size is Medium.\n\nFey\n\nYour creature type is fey, rather than humanoid.\n\nRam\n\nYou can use your head and horns to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMirthful Leaps\n\nWhenever you make a long or high jump, you can roll a d8 and add the number rolled to the number of feet you cover, even when making a standing jump. This extra distance costs movement as normal.\n\nReveler\n\nYou have proficiency in the Performance and Persuasion skills, and you have proficiency with one PHB of your choice.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Sylvan."},
  ["species.satyr.mpmm2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Fey.\n\nRam\n\nYou can use your head and horns to make unarmed strikes. When you hit with them, the strike deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier bludgeoning damage, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\nMirthful Leaps\n\nWhenever you make a long jump or a high jump, you can roll a d8 and add the number rolled to the number of feet you cover, even when making a standing jump. This extra distance costs movement as usual.\n\nReveler\n\nAs an embodiment of revelry, you have proficiency in the Performance and Persuasion skills, and you have proficiency with one PHB of your choice."},
  ["creature.satyr.xmm2024"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 31 (7d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the satyr pushes the target up to 10 feet straight away from itself.\n\nMockery\n\nwis 12, one creature the satyr can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 5 (1d6 + 2) Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.satyr-reveler.mot2014"]={title="Satyr Reveler",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEnthralling Performance\n\nIf the satyr performs for at least 1 minute, it chooses up to four humanoids within 60 feet of it who watched or listened to the entire performance. Each target must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed. While charmed in this way, the target idolizes the satyr and will take part in the satyr's revels. The charmed condition ends for the creature after 1 hour, if it takes any damage, if the satyr attacks the target, or if the target witnesses the satyr attacking or damaging any of the target's allies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSleepless Reveler\n\nMagic can't put the satyr to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes two ram attacks or two shortbow attacks.\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.satyr-revelmaster.xmm2024"]={title="Satyr Revelmaster",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (15d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes three Prance attacks.\n\nPrance\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the satyr's next turn.\n\nFey Melody {@recharge 4}\n\nThe satyr conjures a charming or frightening song. wis 14, each enemy in a 60-foot XPHB originating from the satyr. actSaveFail The target is subjected to the song's effect:\n\n• Charming The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition and uses all its movement to dance in place. The effect ends on the target if it takes any damage.\n\n• Frightening 10 (2d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. If the target ends its turn out of line of sight from the satyr, the condition ends on it."},
  ["creature.satyr-thornbearer.mot2014"]={title="Satyr Thornbearer",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSleepless Reveler\n\nMagic can't put the satyr to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes three ram attacks or three shortbow attacks.\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nHail of Arrows (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe satyr fires an arrow that magically transforms into a flurry of missiles in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) piercing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.sauriv.gos2014"]={title="Sauriv",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 13\n\nWIS 18\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic"},
  ["feat.savage-attacker.phb2014"]={title="Savage Attacker",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nOnce per turn when you roll damage for a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice and use either total."},
  ["feat.savage-attacker.xphb2024"]={title="Savage Attacker",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\nYou've trained to deal particularly damaging strikes. Once per turn when you hit a target with a weapon, you can roll the weapon's damage dice twice and use either roll against the target."},
  ["creature.savid.cos2014"]={title="Savid",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["deity.savras.phb2014"]={title="Savras",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.savras.scag2014"]={title="Savras",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nSavras is a god of divination and fortunetelling. Few people worship him, but many pray to him when performing small rituals of foresight. For example, young men and women sometimes attempt to divine the names of their future spouses by saying a rhyming chant that calls upon Savras while gazing in a mirror.\n\nSavras has no currently active temples in Faerûn, and his shrines are few and far between, tucked away in the corners of libraries and scriptoria. Despite this lack of prominence, certain folk pay regular homage to Savras, including investigators, diviners, judges, and others who have a need to uncover the truth. Such individuals can sometimes be identified by the elaborate staffs they carry in homage to Savras. According to legend, Savras was trapped in Azuth's staff for ages. Azuth eventually freed Savras so long as Savras swore fealty, and today the staff is a potent symbol for those who revere Savras. Devout worshipers take great pains to decorate and embellish their staffs, each hoping that Savras might find it a welcoming place to stop for a time."},
  ["creature.scaladar.wdmm2014"]={title="Scaladar",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 315\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 94 (7d12 + 49)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 1 | WIS 12 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: force, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever the scaladar is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage, and its sting deals an extra 11 (2d10) lightning damage until the end of its next turn.\n\nScaladar Link\n\nThe scaladar knows the location of other scaladar within 100 feet of it, and it can sense when any of them take damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scaladar makes three attacks: two with its claws and one with its sting.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15). The scaladar has two claws, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nSting\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) lightning damage."},
  ["item.scale-mail.phb2014"]={title="Scale Mail",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis armor consists of a coat and leggings (and perhaps a separate skirt) of leather covered with overlapping pieces of metal, much like the scales of a fish. The suit includes gauntlets."},
  ["item.scale-mail.xphb2024"]={title="Scale Mail",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["reward.scaled-toughness.ftd2014"]={title="Scaled Toughness",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYour skin toughens, making you resistant to certain types of physical harm. You gain resistance to piercing and slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.scarab-of-protection.dmg2014"]={title="Scarab of Protection",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nIf you hold this beetle-shaped medallion in your hand for 1 round, an inscription appears on its surface revealing its magical nature. It provides two benefits while it is on your person:\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\n• The scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an undead creature, you can use your reaction to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a successful one. The scarab crumbles into powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended."},
  ["magicitem.scarab-of-protection.xdmg2024"]={title="Scarab of Protection",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis beetle-shaped medallion provides three benefits while it is on your person.\n\nDefense\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to XPHB.\n\nPreservation\n\nThe scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a Necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an Undead, you can take a XPHB to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a successful one. The scarab crumbles into powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended.\n\nSpell Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws against spells."},
  ["creature.scarecrow.mm2014"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 36 (8d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 11 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the scarecrow remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary, inanimate scarecrow.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scarecrow makes two claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of the scarecrow's next turn.\n\nTerrifying Glare\n\nThe scarecrow targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see the scarecrow, the target must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be magically frightened until the end of the scarecrow's next turn. The frightened target is paralyzed."},
  ["creature.scarecrow.wtthc2014"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.scarecrow.xmm2024"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 269\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 11 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFearsome Claw\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the scarecrow's next turn.\n\nTerrifying Glare\n\nwis 11, one creature the scarecrow can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of the scarecrow's next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.scarlet-sentinel.nrh-avitw2014"]={title="Scarlet Sentinel",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-AVitW - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 8\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 6 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["magicitem.scarlet-spellbook.aud2014"]={title="Scarlet Spellbook",subtitle="Item Magico - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nIrregular scraps of red cloth cover this weathered tome. While attuned to this item, you can use it as a Spellbook and an XPHB.\n\nArcane Stamina\n\nWhen you use your Arcane Recovery feature, you also regain XPHB equal to 2d6 plus half your Wizard level (round down).\n\nImproved Spell Recall\n\nWhen you use your Memorize Spell feature, you can replace an additional level 1+ Wizard spell you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell inscribed in this book."},
  ["spell.scatter.xge2024"]={title="Scatter",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 164\n\nThe air quivers around up to five creatures of your choice that you can see within range. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw to resist this spell. You teleport each affected target to an unoccupied space that you can see within 120 feet of you. That space must be on the ground or on a floor."},
  ["vehicle.scavenger.bgdia2014"]={title="Scavenger",subtitle="Veiculo - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nCrushing Wheels\n\nThe Scavenger can move through the space of any Large or smaller creature. When it does, the creature must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or take 16 (3d10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. If the creature was already prone, it takes an extra 16 (3d10) bludgeoning damage. This trait can't be used against a particular creature more than once each turn.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe Scavenger's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nProne Deficiency\n\nIf the Scavenger rolls over and falls prone, it can't right itself and is incapacitated until flipped upright."},
  ["feature.scholar.xphb2024.wizard.base.2"]={title="Scholar",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.scholar-s-anchoring-bangle.au2014"]={title="Scholar's Anchoring Bangle",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis heavy magical bracelet inures your mind against potential distractions. While wearing this bracelet, you gain the following benefits.\n\nDeep Knowledge\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action and make an Intelligence check using a skill in which you have proficiency, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.\n\nSingle-Minded Focus\n\nWhen you fail a Constitution saving throw to maintain XPHB, you can take a XPHB to succeed instead. Once you use this property, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["item.scholar-s-pack.phb2014"]={title="Scholar's Pack",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nIncludes:\n\n• a phb\n\n• a phb of lore\n\n• a phb\n\n• an phb\n\n• 10 phb\n\n• a little bag of sand\n\n• a small knife."},
  ["item.scholar-s-pack.xphb2024"]={title="Scholar's Pack",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Scholar's Pack contains the following items: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, 10 flasks of XPHB, 10 sheets of XPHB, and XPHB."},
  ["creature.scholarly-agent.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Agent",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Shock\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) lightning damage. If the target is a creature, it can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGlyph of Shielding\n\nThe agent adds 2 to its AC against one attack that would hit it. To do so, the agent must be able to see the attacker and have a free hand."},
  ["creature.scholarly-excavator.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Excavator",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSiege Expert\n\nThe excavator deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe excavator makes three Thunderous Warhammer attacks.\n\nThunderous Warhammer\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) thunder damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTelekinetic Toss {@recharge 5}\n\nThe excavator targets one Medium or smaller creature or an object weighing 300 pounds or less that isn't being worn or carried. The target, which must be within 30 feet of the excavator and visible to it, is magically pushed up to 20 feet horizontally in a direction of the excavator's choice. If the target is a creature, it can make a 13 Strength saving throw to resist the effect and is not pushed on a successful save."},
  ["creature.scholarly-mastermind.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Mastermind",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 82 (15d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus three other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mastermind makes two Arcane Shock or Dagger of the Poisoned Mind attacks.\n\nArcane Shock\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h26 (4d10 + 4) lightning damage. If the target is a creature, it can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\nDagger of the Poisoned Mind\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of its next turn."},
  ["subclass.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.0"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Abjuration Savant\n\nPagina: 115\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy an abjuration spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - Arcane Ward\n\nPagina: 115\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can weave magic around yourself for protection. When you cast an spells, you can simultaneously use a strand of the spell's magic to create a magical ward on yourself that lasts until you finish a long rest. The ward has a hit point maximum equal to twice your wizard level + your Intelligence modifier. Whenever you take damage, the ward takes the damage instead. If this damage reduces the ward to 0 hit points, you take any remaining damage.\n\nWhile the ward has 0 hit points, it can't absorb damage, but its magic remains. Whenever you cast an spells, the ward regains a number of hit points equal to twice the level of the spell.\n\nOnce you create the ward, you can't create it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Arcane Ward\n\nNivel 2 - School of Abjuration\n\nPagina: 115\n\nThe School of Abjuration emphasizes magic that blocks, banishes, or protects. Detractors of this school say that its tradition is about denial, negation rather than positive assertion. You understand, however, that ending harmful effects, protecting the weak, and banishing evil influences is anything but a philosophical void. It is a proud and respected vocation.\n\nCalled abjurers, members of this school are sought when baleful spirits require exorcism, when important locations must be guarded against magical spying, and when portals to other planes of existence must be closed.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Abjuration\n\nNivel 6 - Projected Ward\n\nPagina: 115\n\nStarting at 6th level, when a creature that you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to cause your Arcane Ward to absorb that damage. If this damage reduces the ward to 0 hit points, the warded creature takes any remaining damage.\n\nNivel 6 - Projected Ward\n\nNivel 10 - Improved Abjuration\n\nPagina: 115\n\nBeginning at 10th level, when you cast an abjuration spell that requires you to make an ability check as a part of casting that spell (as in counterspell and dispel magic), you add your proficiency bonus to that ability check.\n\nNivel 14 - Spell Resistance\n\nPagina: 115\n\nStarting at 14th level, you have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\nFurthermore, you have resistance against the damage of spells."},
  ["feature.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.2"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\nThe School of Abjuration emphasizes magic that blocks, banishes, or protects. Detractors of this school say that its tradition is about denial, negation rather than positive assertion. You understand, however, that ending harmful effects, protecting the weak, and banishing evil influences is anything but a philosophical void. It is a proud and respected vocation.\n\nCalled abjurers, members of this school are sought when baleful spirits require exorcism, when important locations must be guarded against magical spying, and when portals to other planes of existence must be closed."},
  ["feature.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.3"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.0"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Conjuration Savant\n\nPagina: 116\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a conjuration spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - Minor Conjuration\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 2nd level when you select this school, you can use your action to conjure up an inanimate object in your hand or on the ground in an unoccupied space that you can see within 10 feet of you. This object can be no larger than 3 feet on a side and weigh no more than 10 pounds, and its form must be that of a nonmagical object that you have seen. The object is visibly magical, radiating dim light out to 5 feet.\n\nThe object disappears after 1 hour, when you use this feature again, if it takes any damage, or if it deals any damage.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Conjuration\n\nPagina: 116\n\nAs a conjurer, you favor spells that produce objects and creatures out of thin air. You can conjure billowing clouds of killing fog or summon creatures from elsewhere to fight on your behalf. As your mastery grows, you learn spells of transportation and can teleport yourself across vast distances, even to other planes of existence, in an instant.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Conjuration\n\nNivel 6 - Benign Transposition\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your action to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. Alternatively, you can choose a space within range that is occupied by a Small or Medium creature. If that creature is willing, you both teleport, swapping places.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest or you cast a conjuration spell of 1st level or higher.\n\nNivel 6 - Benign Transposition\n\nNivel 10 - Focused Conjuration\n\nPagina: 116\n\nBeginning at 10th level, while you are concentration on a conjuration spell, your concentration can't be broken as a result of taking damage.\n\nNivel 14 - Durable Summons\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 14th level, any creature that you summon or create with a conjuration spell has 30 temporary hit points."},
  ["feature.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.2"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nAs a conjurer, you favor spells that produce objects and creatures out of thin air. You can conjure billowing clouds of killing fog or summon creatures from elsewhere to fight on your behalf. As your mastery grows, you learn spells of transportation and can teleport yourself across vast distances, even to other planes of existence, in an instant."},
  ["feature.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.3"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.0"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Divination Savant\n\nPagina: 116\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a divination spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - Portent\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 2nd level when you choose this school, glimpses of the future begin to press in on your awareness. When you finish a long rest, roll two d20s and record the numbers rolled. You can replace any attack roll, saving throw, or ability check made by you or a creature that you can see with one of these foretelling rolls. You must choose to do so before the roll, and you can replace a roll in this way only once per turn.\n\nEach foretelling roll can be used only once. When you finish a long rest, you lose any unused foretelling rolls.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Divination\n\nPagina: 116\n\nThe counsel of a diviner is sought by royalty and commoners alike, for all seek a clearer understanding of the past, present, and future. As a diviner, you strive to part the veils of space, time, and consciousness so that you can see clearly. You work to master spells of discernment, remote viewing, supernatural knowledge, and foresight.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Divination\n\nNivel 6 - Expert Divination\n\nPagina: 116\n\nBeginning at 6th level, casting divination spells comes so easily to you that it expends only a fraction of your spellcasting efforts. When you cast a spells using a spell slot, you regain one expended spell slot. The slot you regain must be of a level lower than the spell you cast and can't be higher than 5th level.\n\nNivel 10 - The Third Eye\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 10th level, you can use your action to increase your powers of perception. When you do so, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you are incapacitated or you take a short or long rest. You can't use the feature again until you finish a rest.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou gain darkvision out to a range of 60 feet.\n\nEthereal Sight\n\nYou can see into the Ethereal Plane within 60 feet of you.\n\nGreater Comprehension\n\nYou can read any language.\n\nSee Invisibility\n\nYou can see invisible creatures and objects within 10 feet of you that are within line of sight.\n\nNivel 14 - Greater Portent\n\nPagina: 116\n\nStarting at 14th level, the visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. You roll three d20s for your Portent feature, rather than two."},
  ["feature.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.2"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nThe counsel of a diviner is sought by royalty and commoners alike, for all seek a clearer understanding of the past, present, and future. As a diviner, you strive to part the veils of space, time, and consciousness so that you can see clearly. You work to master spells of discernment, remote viewing, supernatural knowledge, and foresight."},
  ["feature.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.3"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.0"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Enchantment Savant\n\nPagina: 117\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy an enchantment spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - Hypnotic Gaze\n\nPagina: 117\n\nStarting at 2nd level when you choose this school, your soft words and enchanting gaze can magically enthrall another creature. As an action, choose one creature that you can see within 5 feet of you. If the target can see or hear you, it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your wizard spell save DC or be charmed by you until the end of your next turn. The charmed creature's speed drops to 0, and the creature is incapacitated and visibly dazed.\n\nOn subsequent turns, you can use your action to maintain this effect, extending its duration until the end of your next turn. However, the effect ends if you move more than 5 feet away from the creature, if the creature can neither see nor hear you, or if the creature takes damage.\n\nOnce the effect ends, or if the creature succeeds on its initial saving throw against this effect, you can't use this feature on that creature again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Hypnotic Gaze\n\nNivel 2 - School of Enchantment\n\nPagina: 117\n\nAs a member of the School of Enchantment, you have honed your ability to magically entrance and beguile other people and monsters. Some enchanters are peacemakers who bewitch the violent to lay down their arms and charm the cruel into showing mercy. Others are tyrants who magically bind the unwilling into their service. Most enchanters fall somewhere in between.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Enchantment\n\nNivel 6 - Instinctive Charm\n\nPagina: 117\n\nBeginning at 6th level, when a creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll against you, you can use your reaction to divert the attack, provided that another creature is within the attack's range. The attacker must make a Wisdom saving throw against your wizard spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker must target the creature that is closest to it, not including you or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target. On a successful save, you can't use this feature on the attacker again until you finish a long rest.\n\nYou must choose to use this feature before knowing whether the attack hits or misses. Creatures that can't be charmed are immune to this effect.\n\nNivel 6 - Instinctive Charm\n\nNivel 10 - Split Enchantment\n\nPagina: 117\n\nStarting at 10th level, when you cast an enchantment spell of 1st level or higher that targets only one creature, you can have it target a second creature.\n\nNivel 14 - Alter Memories\n\nPagina: 117\n\nAt 14th level, you gain the ability to make a creature unaware of your magical influence on it. When you cast an enchantment spell to charm one or more creatures, you can alter one creature's understanding so that it remains unaware of being charmed.\n\nAdditionally, once before the spell expires, you can use your action to try to make the chosen creature forget some of the time it spent charmed. The creature must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw against your wizard spell save DC or lose a number of hours of its memories equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1). You can make the creature forget less time, and the amount of time can't exceed the duration of your enchantment spell."},
  ["feature.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.2"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nAs a member of the School of Enchantment, you have honed your ability to magically entrance and beguile other people and monsters. Some enchanters are peacemakers who bewitch the violent to lay down their arms and charm the cruel into showing mercy. Others are tyrants who magically bind the unwilling into their service. Most enchanters fall somewhere in between."},
  ["feature.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.3"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.0"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Evocation Savant\n\nPagina: 117\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy an evocation spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Evocation\n\nPagina: 117\n\nYou focus your study on magic that creates powerful elemental effects such as bitter cold, searing flame, rolling thunder, crackling lightning, and burning acid. Some evokers find employment in military forces, serving as artillery to blast enemy armies from afar. Others use their spectacular power to protect the weak, while some seek their own gain as bandits, adventurers, or aspiring tyrants.\n\nNivel 2 - Sculpt Spells\n\nPagina: 117\n\nBeginning at 2nd level, you can create pockets of relative safety within the effects of your evocation spells. When you cast an evocation spell that affects other creatures that you can see, you can choose a number of them equal to 1 + the spell's level. The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their saving throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Evocation\n\nNivel 6 - Potent Cantrip\n\nPagina: 117\n\nStarting at 6th level, your damaging cantrips affect even creatures that avoid the brunt of the effect. When a creature succeeds on a saving throw against your cantrip, the creature takes half the cantrip's damage (if any) but suffers no additional effect from the cantrip.\n\nNivel 10 - Empowered Evocation\n\nPagina: 117\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of any wizard evocation spell you cast.\n\nNivel 14 - Overchannel\n\nPagina: 117\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can increase the power of your simpler spells. When you cast a wizard spell of 1st through 5th-level that deals damage, you can deal maximum damage with that spell.\n\nThe first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a long rest, you take 2d12 necrotic damage for each level of the spell, immediately after you cast it. Each time you use this feature again before finishing a long rest, the necrotic damage per spell level increases by 1d12. This damage ignores resistance and immunity."},
  ["feature.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.2"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nYou focus your study on magic that creates powerful elemental effects such as bitter cold, searing flame, rolling thunder, crackling lightning, and burning acid. Some evokers find employment in military forces, serving as artillery to blast enemy armies from afar. Others use their spectacular power to protect the weak, while some seek their own gain as bandits, adventurers, or aspiring tyrants."},
  ["feature.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.3"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.0"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Illusion Savant\n\nPagina: 118\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy an illusion spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - Improved Minor Illusion\n\nPagina: 118\n\nWhen you choose this school at 2nd level, you learn the minor illusion cantrip. If you already know this cantrip, you learn a different wizard cantrip of your choice. The cantrip doesn't count against your number of cantrips known.\n\nWhen you cast minor illusion, you can create both a sound and an image with a single casting of the spell.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Illusion\n\nPagina: 118\n\nYou focus your studies on magic that dazzles the senses, befuddles the mind, and tricks even the wisest folk. Your magic is subtle, but the illusions crafted by your keen mind make the impossible seem real. Some illusionists—including many gnome wizards—are benign tricksters who use their spells to entertain. Others are more sinister masters of deception, using their illusions to frighten and fool others for their personal gain.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Illusion\n\nNivel 6 - Malleable Illusions\n\nPagina: 118\n\nStarting at 6th level, when you cast an illusion spell that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, you can use your action to change the nature of that illusion (using the spell's normal parameters for the illusion), provided that you can see the illusion.\n\nNivel 10 - Illusory Self\n\nPagina: 118\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you can create an illusory duplicate of yourself as an instant, almost instinctual reaction to danger. When a creature makes an attack roll against you, you can use your reaction to interpose the illusory duplicate between the attacker and yourself. The attack automatically misses you, then the illusion dissipates.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 14 - Illusory Reality\n\nPagina: 118\n\nBy 14th level, you have learned the secret of weaving shadow magic into your illusions to give them a semi-reality. When you cast an illusion spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose one inanimate, nonmagical object that is part of the illusion and make that object real. You can do this on your turn as a bonus action while the spell is ongoing. The object remains real for 1 minute. For example, you can create an illusion of a bridge over a chasm and then make it real long enough for your allies to cross.\n\nThe object can't deal damage or otherwise directly harm anyone."},
  ["feature.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.2"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nYou focus your studies on magic that dazzles the senses, befuddles the mind, and tricks even the wisest folk. Your magic is subtle, but the illusions crafted by your keen mind make the impossible seem real. Some illusionists—including many gnome wizards—are benign tricksters who use their spells to entertain. Others are more sinister masters of deception, using their illusions to frighten and fool others for their personal gain."},
  ["feature.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.3"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.0"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Grim Harvest\n\nPagina: 118\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain the ability to reap life energy from creatures you kill with your spells. Once per turn when you kill one or more creatures with a spell of 1st level or higher, you regain hit points equal to twice the spell's level, or three times its level if the spell belongs to the spells. You don't gain this benefit for killing constructs or undead.\n\nNivel 2 - Necromancy Savant\n\nPagina: 118\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a necromancy spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Necromancy\n\nPagina: 118\n\nThe School of Necromancy explores the cosmic forces of life, death, and undeath. As you focus your studies in this tradition, you learn to manipulate the energy that animates all living things. As you progress, you learn to sap the life force from a creature as your magic destroys its body, transforming that vital energy into magical power you can manipulate.\n\nMost people see necromancers as menacing, or even villainous, due to the close association with death. Not all necromancers are evil, but the forces they manipulate are considered taboo by many societies.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Necromancy\n\nNivel 6 - Undead Thralls\n\nPagina: 118\n\nAt 6th level, you add the animate dead spell to your spellbook if it is not there already. When you cast animate dead, you can target one additional corpse or pile of bones, creating another zombie or skeleton, as appropriate.\n\nWhenever you create an undead using a necromancy spell, it has additional benefits:\n\n• The creature's hit point maximum is increased by an amount equal to your wizard level.\n\n• The creature adds your proficiency bonus to its weapon damage rolls.\n\nNivel 10 - Inured to Undeath\n\nPagina: 118\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you have resistance to necrotic damage, and your hit point maximum can't be reduced. You have spent so much time dealing with undead and the forces that animate them that you have become inured to some of their worst effects.\n\nNivel 10 - Inured to Undeath\n\nNivel 14 - Command Undead\n\nPagina: 118\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can use magic to bring undead under your control, even those created by other wizards. As an action, you can choose one undead that you can see within 60 feet of you. That creature must make a Charisma saving throw against your wizard spell save DC. If it succeeds, you can't use this feature on it again. If it fails, it becomes friendly to you and obeys your commands until you use this feature again.\n\nIntelligent undead are harder to control in this way. If the target has an Intelligence of 8 or higher, it has advantage on the saving throw. If it fails the saving throw and has an Intelligence of 12 or higher, it can repeat the saving throw at the end of every hour until it succeeds and breaks free.\n\nNivel 14 - Command Undead"},
  ["feature.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.2"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nThe School of Necromancy explores the cosmic forces of life, death, and undeath. As you focus your studies in this tradition, you learn to manipulate the energy that animates all living things. As you progress, you learn to sap the life force from a creature as your magic destroys its body, transforming that vital energy into magical power you can manipulate.\n\nMost people see necromancers as menacing, or even villainous, due to the close association with death. Not all necromancers are evil, but the forces they manipulate are considered taboo by many societies."},
  ["feature.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.3"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.0"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Minor Alchemy\n\nPagina: 119\n\nStarting at 2nd level when you select this school, you can temporarily alter the physical properties of one nonmagical object, changing it from one substance into another. You perform a special alchemical procedure on one object composed entirely of wood, stone (but not a gemstone), iron, copper, or silver, transforming it into a different one of those materials. For each 10 minutes you spend performing the procedure, you can transform up to 1 cubic foot of material. After 1 hour, or until you lose your concentration (as if you were concentration on a spell), the material reverts to its original substance.\n\nNivel 2 - School of Transmutation\n\nPagina: 119\n\nYou are a student of spells that modify energy and matter. To you, the world is not a fixed thing, but eminently mutable, and you delight in being an agent of change. You wield the raw stuff of creation and learn to alter both physical forms and mental qualities. Your magic gives you the tools to become a smith on reality's forge.\n\nSome transmuters are tinkerers and pranksters, turning people into toads and transforming copper into silver for fun and occasional profit. Others pursue their magical studies with deadly seriousness, seeking the power of the gods to make and destroy worlds.\n\nNivel 2 - Transmutation Savant\n\nPagina: 119\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a transmutation spell into your spellbook is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - School of Transmutation\n\nNivel 6 - Transmuter's Stone\n\nPagina: 119\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can spend 8 hours creating a transmuter's stone that stores transmutation magic. You can benefit from the stone yourself or give it to another creature. A creature gains a benefit of your choice as long as the stone is in the creature's possession. When you create the stone, choose the benefit from the following options:\n\n• Darkvision out to a range of 60 feet, as described in chapter 8.\n\n• An increase to speed of 10 feet while the creature is unencumbered.\n\n• Proficiency in Constitution saving throws.\n\n• Resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (your choice whenever you choose this benefit).\n\nEach time you cast a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher, you can change the effect of your stone if the stone is on your person.\n\nIf you create a new transmuter's stone, the previous one ceases to function.\n\nNivel 10 - Shapechanger\n\nPagina: 119\n\nAt 10th level, you add the polymorph spell to your spellbook, if it is not there already. You can cast polymorph without expending a spell slot. When you do so, you can target only yourself and transform into a bestiary.\n\nOnce you cast polymorph in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a short or long rest, though you can still cast it normally using an available spell slot.\n\nNivel 14 - Master Transmuter\n\nPagina: 119\n\nStarting at 14th level, you can use your action to consume the reserve of transmutation magic stored within your transmuter's stone in a single burst. When you do so, choose one of the following effects. Your transmuter's stone is destroyed and can't be remade until you finish a long rest.\n\nMajor Transformation\n\nYou can transmute one nonmagical object—no larger than a 5-foot cube—into another nonmagical object of similar size and mass and of equal or lesser value. You must spend 10 minutes handling the object to transform it.\n\nPanacea\n\nYou remove all curses, diseases, and poisons affecting a creature that you touch with the transmuter's stone. The creature also regains all its hit points.\n\nRestore Life\n\nYou cast the raise dead spell on a creature you touch with the transmuter's stone, without expending a spell slot or needing to have the spell in your spellbook.\n\nRestore Youth\n\nYou touch the transmuter's stone to a willing creature, and that creature's apparent age is reduced by 3d10 years, to a minimum of 13 years. This effect doesn't extend the creature's lifespan."},
  ["feature.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.2"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nYou are a student of spells that modify energy and matter. To you, the world is not a fixed thing, but eminently mutable, and you delight in being an agent of change. You wield the raw stuff of creation and learn to alter both physical forms and mental qualities. Your magic gives you the tools to become a smith on reality's forge.\n\nSome transmuters are tinkerers and pranksters, turning people into toads and transforming copper into silver for fun and occasional profit. Others pursue their magical studies with deadly seriousness, seeking the power of the gods to make and destroy worlds."},
  ["feature.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.3"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["item.scimitar.phb2014"]={title="Scimitar",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.scimitar.xphb2024"]={title="Scimitar",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.scimitar-of-speed.dmg2014"]={title="Scimitar of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a bonus action on each of your turns."},
  ["magicitem.scimitar-of-speed.xdmg2024"]={title="Scimitar of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a XPHB on each of your turns."},
  ["creature.scion-of-grolantor.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Grolantor",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 402 (23d20 + 161)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 15 | WIS 21 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Great Tree Club attack and two Slam attacks, or it makes three Boulder attacks.\n\nGreat Tree Club\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h30 (4d10 + 8) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 23 Strength saving throw or be pushed horizontally up to 100 feet straight away from the scion and have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h26 (4d8 + 8) force damage.\n\nBoulder\n\nrw 15 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h27 (3d12 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nInhale {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion inhales a vortex of air in a 120-foot line that is 15 feet wide. Each creature in that area that is Huge or smaller must succeed on a 23 Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 120 feet straight toward the scion and be swallowed. A swallowed creature has the restrained condition, has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the scion, and takes 24 (7d6) force damage at the start of each of the scion's turns.\n\nThe scion's stomach can hold up to two creatures at a time. If the scion takes 60 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the scion must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls in a space within 10 feet of the scion and has the prone condition. If the scion dies, any swallowed creature no longer has the restrained condition and can escape from the corpse using 15 feet of movement, exiting with the prone condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFeed\n\nImmediately after taking damage, if it has at least one creature swallowed, the scion deals 10 (3d6) force damage to each swallowed creature and regains 10 hit points."},
  ["creature.scion-of-memnor.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Memnor",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 656 (32d20 + 320)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 18 | CON 30 | INT 24 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe scion doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Cloud Morningstar or Wind Javelin, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nCloud Morningstar\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) force damage plus 22 (4d10) thunder damage.\n\nWind Javelin\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h42 (5d12 + 10) thunder damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h28 (4d8 + 10) force damage.\n\nThunderous Vortex {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion magically creates a vortex of wind in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on a point it can see within 120 feet of itself. Each creature in the sphere must succeed on a 24 Strength saving throw or be pulled straight toward the sphere's center, ending in an unoccupied space as close as possible to the center. Then a burst of thunder erupts in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on the same point. Each creature in that area takes 52 (8d12) thunder damage and must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nFog of Deception\n\nThe scion conjures a magical cloud that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point it can see within 90 feet of itself. Each creature in that area must make a 24 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature has the charmed condition until the end of its next turn. While it has the charmed condition, the creature must use its action to make a melee attack against a creature other than itself of the scion's choice. If no creature is within its reach, the affected creature makes a ranged attack against a creature of the scion's choice, throwing its weapon if necessary. On a successful save, a creature is immune to the scion's Fog of Deception for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.scion-of-skoraeus.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Skoraeus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 20 | CON 26 | INT 19 | WIS 24 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Crystal Club attack and two Slam attacks, then uses Entombing Grasp if available. Alternatively, the scion makes two Runic Boulder attacks.\n\nCrystal Club\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h35 (4d12 + 9) bludgeoning damage. homThe scion can cause the club to flare with bright light, and the target must succeed on a 22 Constitution saving throw or take 18 (4d8) radiant damage and have the blinded condition until the start of the scion's next turn.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h31 (4d10 + 9) force damage.\n\nRunic Boulder\n\nrw 16 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h27 (4d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage. homThe boulder explodes. The target and each creature within 30 feet of it must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 19 (3d12) force damage and has the prone condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\nEntombing Grasp {@recharge}\n\nThe scion wreathes its hand in petrifying magic and touches one Huge or smaller creature it can see within 20 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 24 Dexterity saving throw or take 28 (8d6) force damage and have the grappled condition (escape 19). At the start of the scion's next turn, if the target is still grappled, the target has the petrified condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration."},
  ["creature.scion-of-stronmaus.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Stronmaus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 656 (32d20 + 320)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 80, swim: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 20 | CON 30 | INT 26 | WIS 28 | CHA 24\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe scion doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Lightning Sword or Hailstone, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nLightning Sword\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage plus 22 (4d10) lightning damage.\n\nHailstone\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVengeful Storm {@recharge}\n\nThe scion conjures a churning storm cloud in a 30-foot-radius, 10-foot-tall cylinder centered on a point within 120 feet of itself. The cloud's area is Vision and Light. The cloud lasts for 1 minute, until the scion dies, or when the scion uses this bonus action again.\n\nWhen the cloud appears, and as a bonus action on later turns, the scion can move the cloud up to 30 feet and cause one of the following effects in a 30-foot-radius, 120-foot-high cylinder directly below it; the scion can't choose the same effect two rounds in a row:\n\nAcid Rain\n\nThe cloud rains acid. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or be covered in acid for 1 minute or until a creature uses its action to remove the acid from itself or another creature. A creature covered in the acid takes 26 (4d12) acid damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nFreezing Storm\n\nShards of ice pelt down, and freezing wind fills the area. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 28 (8d6) cold damage and be hindered by ice formations for 1 minute or until it or another creature within reach of it uses an action to break away the ice. A creature hindered by ice has its speed reduced to 0.\n\nLightning Bolts\n\nBolts of lightning strike down. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) lightning damage and have the stunned condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.scion-of-surtur.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Surtur",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 546 (28d20 + 252)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 17 | CON 28 | INT 21 | WIS 24 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Lava Blade or Lava Ball, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nLava Blade\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) slashing damage plus 18 (4d8) fire damage.\n\nLava Ball\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h29 (3d12 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) fire damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h28 (4d8 + 10) force damage.\n\nLava Wave {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion emits a wave of lava from its blade, hands, or mouth in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 60 (11d10) fire damage and has the restrained condition from being embedded in hardening rock. A creature can make a 25 Strength (Athletics) check as an action, freeing itself or a creature within reach from the rock on a success. The rock has AC 17 and 40 hit points, and it is immune to fire, poison, and psychic damage. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 26 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration.\n\nIncendiary Smoke\n\nThe scion causes smoke and white-hot embers to billow from its skin, filling a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself that moves with it. While the scion's skin billows smoke, ranged attacks against the scion are made with disadvantage. A creature that moves into the smoke for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or take 14 (4d6) fire damage. The scion's skin stops billowing smoke after 1 minute, when the scion dies, or when the scion uses this bonus action to stop the smoke."},
  ["feat.scion-of-the-outer-planes.sato2014"]={title="Scion of the Outer Planes",subtitle="Feat - SatO - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nYour connection to an Outer Plane infuses you with the energy there. Choose a type of plane listed in the Planar Infusion table. Your choice gives you resistance to a damage type and the ability to cast a cantrip, as specified in the table. You can cast this cantrip without material components, and your spellcasting ability for it is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).\n\nPlane | Damage Resistance | Cantrip\n\nChaotic Outer Plane | Poison | Minor illusion\n\nEvil Outer Plane | Necrotic | Chill touch\n\nGood Outer Plane | Radiant | Sacred flame\n\nLawful Outer Plane | Force | Guidance\n\nThe Outlands | Psychic | Mage hand"},
  ["subclass.scion-of-the-three.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.0"]={title="Scion of the Three",subtitle="Subclasse - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Bloodthirst\n\nPagina: 23\n\nWhen an enemy you can see within 30 feet of yourself takes damage and is XPHB after taking that damage but not killed outright, you can take a XPHB and XPHB to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of that enemy. You can then make one melee attack. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Allegiance\n\nPagina: 23\n\nChoose one of the Dead Three: Faerûnian, Faerûnian, or Faerûnian. You gain XPHB to one type of damage and the ability to cast a cantrip, as detailed in the table below; Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for this cantrip. When you finish a XPHB, you can change your choice.\n\nGod | Damage Resistance | Cantrip\n\nFaerûnian | Psychic | XPHB\n\nFaerûnian | Poison | XPHB\n\nFaerûnian | Necrotic | XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Scion of the Three\n\nPagina: 23\n\nBecome a Gruesome Agent of Malice\n\nA Scion of the Three draws power from a group of malevolent gods known as the Dead Three: Faerûnian, deity of tyranny; Faerûnian, deity of violence and murder; and Faerûnian, deity of death. While some Rogues of this subclass pledge themselves ardently to those three macabre gods, others find themselves thrust on this path by a curse. Either way, a scion's power manifests as various occult gifts, as well as an uncanny talent for striking and terrifying foes.\n\nScions of the Three are most common in Baldur's Gate, where the Dead Three have long competed for influence over mortal hearts. Underground cults to Faerûnian, Faerûnian, and Faerûnian often count Scions of the Three among their most useful agents. Outside Baldur's Gate, secular thieves' guilds such as the Shadow Thieves of Amn or Xanathar's guild in Waterdeep might cautiously call on a Scion of the Three to undertake an especially violent contract.\n\nNivel 9 - Strike Fear\n\nPagina: 23\n\nYou gain the following Rogue option.\n\nTerrify (Cost: 1d6)\n\nThe target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or it has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While the target is Frightened in this way, you have XPHB on attack rolls against the target.\n\nThe XPHB target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nNivel 13 - Aura of Malevolence\n\nPagina: 24\n\nYou radiate malignant power associated with one of the Dead Three. When you use Rogue and teleport, each creature of your choice within 10 feet of either the space you left or your destination space (your choice) takes damage equal to your Intelligence modifier; the damage type is the same as the damage XPHB granted by your choice in the Dread Allegiance feature. Damage dealt by this feature ignores XPHB.\n\nNivel 17 - Dread Incarnate\n\nPagina: 24\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCutthroat\n\nYou regain one expended use of Rogue when you finish a XPHB.\n\nMurderous Intent\n\nWhen you roll for your Rogue damage, you can treat a roll of a 1 or 2 on the die as a 3."},
  ["feature.scion-of-the-three.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.3"]={title="Scion of the Three",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nBecome a Gruesome Agent of Malice\n\nA Scion of the Three draws power from a group of malevolent gods known as the Dead Three: Faerûnian, deity of tyranny; Faerûnian, deity of violence and murder; and Faerûnian, deity of death. While some Rogues of this subclass pledge themselves ardently to those three macabre gods, others find themselves thrust on this path by a curse. Either way, a scion's power manifests as various occult gifts, as well as an uncanny talent for striking and terrifying foes.\n\nScions of the Three are most common in Baldur's Gate, where the Dead Three have long competed for influence over mortal hearts. Underground cults to Faerûnian, Faerûnian, and Faerûnian often count Scions of the Three among their most useful agents. Outside Baldur's Gate, secular thieves' guilds such as the Shadow Thieves of Amn or Xanathar's guild in Waterdeep might cautiously call on a Scion of the Three to undertake an especially violent contract."},
  ["creature.scion-of-thrym.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Thrym",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 499 (27d20 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 16 | CON 27 | INT 17 | WIS 20 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: cold\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Ice Axe and two Slam attacks, or it makes two Glacier Throw attacks.\n\nIce Axe\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) force damage.\n\nGlacier Throw\n\nrw 17 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) cold damage, and the target must succeed on a 25 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nGlacial Upheaval {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion digs its hands into the ground at a point it can see within 30 feet of itself and launches a magically conjured mass of ice into the air. Each creature other than the scion in a 30-foot-radius, 100-foot-high cylinder centered on that point must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 36 (8d8) bludgeoning damage plus 19 (3d12) cold damage and is pushed vertically to the top of the cylinder, at which point the creature falls. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and is pushed to the nearest unoccupied space outside the cylinder with no additional effects.\n\nAt the start of the scion's next turn, a mass of ice plummets to the ground on a point the scion can see within 60 feet of the point the scion dug its hands into. Each creature in a 30-foot-radius, 100-foot-high cylinder centered on that point must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration."},
  ["magicitem.scissors-of-shadow-snipping.wbtw2014"]={title="Scissors of Shadow Snipping",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nAs an action, you make a few snips with these iron shears and cause the shadow of a Humanoid creature you can see within 5 feet of you to detach from its source. If the creature is unwilling to give up its shadow, it can make a 15 Charisma saving throw, retaining its shadow on a success. Whether or not the shadow is snipped, this property of the scissors can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nThe detached shadow is rooted to the spot where it was snipped until you use a bonus action to cause it to behave in one of the following ways, either of which is possible only if you can see the shadow:\n\n• You control the shadow's movements and can make the shadow move up to 30 feet across a solid or liquid surface, in any direction you choose (including along vertical surfaces), provided it remains within your sight at all times. The shadow is harmless and unable to be harmed, and it is invisible in darkness. It can't speak, and it doesn't require air, sleep, or nourishment.\n\n• You can relinquish control of the shadow, at which point it becomes autonomous and behaves as the DM wishes. It uses the shadow stat block in the Monster Manual, but its creature type is Fey instead of Undead. A creature whose Strength is reduced to 0 by this shadow's Strength Drain attack does not die but falls unconscious instead. The creature regains consciousness and all its Strength after finishing a short or long rest.\n\nA creature whose shadow has detached from it is cursed. If a shadowless creature is subjected to any spell that ends a curse, or if its detached shadow is reduced to 0 hit points, the detached shadow disappears, and the creature regains its normal shadow instantly."},
  ["creature.scorchbringer-guard.ggr2014"]={title="Scorchbringer Guard",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 9 | CHA 10\n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nExplosive Tank\n\nWhen the guard dies, or if it rolls a 1 when checking whether its Scorchbringer action recharges, the tank on its back explodes in a 10-foot radius sphere. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The explosion ignites flammable objects that aren't being worn or carried, and it destroys the scorchbringer.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLight Hammer\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nScorchbringer {@recharge 4}\n\nThe guard's scorchbringer spouts a stream of flame in a line that is 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["spell.scorching-ray.phb2014"]={title="Scorching Ray",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\nYou create three rays of fire and hurl them at targets within range. You can hurl them at one target or several.\n\nMake a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 fire damage."},
  ["spell.scorching-ray.xphb2024"]={title="Scorching Ray",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nYou hurl three fiery rays. You can hurl them at one target within range or at several. Make a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 Fire damage."},
  ["feature.scornful-rebuke.xge2024.paladin.conquest.15"]={title="Scornful Rebuke",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 37\n\nStarting at 15th level, those who dare to strike you are psychically punished for their audacity. Whenever a creature hits you with an attack, that creature takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1) if you're not incapacitated."},
  ["creature.scorpion.mm2014"]={title="Scorpion",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 337\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 1 (1d4 - 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 11 | CON 8 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 2\n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSting\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h1 piercing damage, and the target must make a 9 Constitution saving throw, taking 4 (1d8) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.scorpion.xmm2024"]={title="Scorpion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 369\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 1 (1d4 - 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 11 | CON 8 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 2\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSting\n\nm 2, reach 5 ft. h1 Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.scorpion-armor.toa2014"]={title="Scorpion Armor",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis suit of plate armor is fashioned from giant scorpion chitin. While wearing this armor, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• The armor improves your combat readiness, granting you a +5 bonus to initiative as long as you aren't incapacitated.\n\n• The armor doesn't impose disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.\n\n• The armor doesn't impose disadvantage on saving throws made to resist the effects of extreme heat (see chapter 5 of the Dungeon Master's Guide).\n\nCurse\n\nThis armor is cursed. Whenever you don or doff it, you must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 100 (10d10 + 45) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Only a wish spell can remove the armor's curse."},
  ["item.scorpion-ship.aag2014"]={title="Scorpion Ship",subtitle="Item - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nRaridade: none\n\nScorpion ships are archaic metal warships that have never lost their popularity, largely because of their versatility. Articulated legs enable a scorpion ship to land safely on the ground and move across a solid surface at a walking speed of 30 feet. The ship can't float on water, however. A ballista is mounted on the top deck, and a mangonel is perched on the end of the tail. The ship's two claws are relatively inefficient in combat, but a claw that grabs a creature can quickly take it out of action."},
  ["vehicle.scorpion-ship.aag2014"]={title="Scorpion Ship",subtitle="Veiculo - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 42"},
  ["magicitem.scourge-of-shadow.coa2014"]={title="Scourge of Shadow",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 275\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nSaid to be a gift to Glasya from Asmodeus, the Scourge of Shadow is a multi-headed whip constructed from infernal iron. The scourge is nigh-in- destructible, and Glasya carries it with her wherever she goes. When she wields the whip in battle, it shrouds her in an aura of shadow.\n\nThe Scourge of Shadow is a magic whip. You have a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this weapon, and it does 3d4 slashing damage instead of its regular damage. When you hit a good aligned creature with it, that creatures takes an extra 4d4 necrotic damage.\n\nWhenever an unattuned creature attacks with the weapon, it deals 2d4 necrotic damage, ignoring resistances and immunities, to them, but otherwise functions normally.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Scourge of Shadow has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\nKeen\n\nThe whip scores a critical on a roll of 18, 19, or 20. When it scores a critical, its damage dice are upgraded to 3d6 instead of 3d4 for the duration of the attack. If attacking a good aligned creature, or attacking with the weapon unattuned, the necrotic damage dice are also increased to a d6 instead of a d4.\n\nFast Reflexes\n\nWhile attuned to the Scourge of Shadow, you gain advantage on initiative rolls, and you add your Charisma and Dexterity modifiers to the roll. You may use either your Strength, Dexterity, or Charisma modifier for the attack and damage rolls (the same modifier must be used for both attack and damage).\n\nVeil of Shadow\n\nYou're protected by a field of shadow that makes you resistant to radiant and necrotic damage. While in Vision and Light or darkness you gain blindsight out to 60 feet and Dexterity (Stealth) checks are made with advantage.\n\nDestroying the Scourge\n\nThough the process is known only to Glasya and Asmodeus, the Scourge of Shadow can be destroyed. It must be taken to the Pit of Fire in Phlegethos. The scourge, along with the body of an archdevil, must be thrown into the Hellfire together. As they hit the flames, a spell of Darkness must be cast at 9th level on the scourge. If each part of the ritual is performed correctly, the whip disintegrates within the Hellfire."},
  ["creature.scout.mm2014"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 349\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Sight\n\nThe scout has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, ranged 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["subclass.scout.xge2024.rogue.scout.0"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Scout\n\nPagina: 47\n\nYou are skilled in stealth and surviving far from the streets of a city, allowing you to scout ahead of your companions during expeditions. Rogues who embrace this archetype are at home in the wilderness and among barbarians and rangers, and many Scouts serve as the eyes and ears of war bands. Ambusher, spy, bounty hunter—these are just a few of the roles that Scouts assume as they range the world.\n\nNivel 3 - Skirmisher\n\nPagina: 47\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you are difficult to pin down during a fight. You can move up to half your speed as a reaction when an enemy ends its turn within 5 feet of you. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nNivel 3 - Survivalist\n\nPagina: 47\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency in the Nature and Survival skills if you don't already have it. Your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make that uses either of those proficiencies.\n\nNivel 3 - Survivalist\n\nNivel 9 - Superior Mobility\n\nPagina: 47\n\nAt 9th level, your walking speed increases by 10 feet. If you have a climbing or swimming speed, this increase applies to that speed as well.\n\nNivel 9 - Superior Mobility\n\nNivel 13 - Ambush Master\n\nPagina: 47\n\nStarting at 13th level, you excel at leading ambushes and acting first in a fight.\n\nYou have advantage on initiative rolls. In addition, the first creature you hit during the first round of a combat becomes easier for you and others to strike; attack rolls against that target have advantage until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Sudden Strike\n\nPagina: 47\n\nStarting at 17th level, you can strike with deadly speed. If you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make one additional attack as a bonus action. This attack can benefit from your Sneak Attack even if you have already used it this turn, but you can't use your Sneak Attack against the same target more than once in a turn."},
  ["feature.scout.xge2024.rogue.scout.3"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 47\n\nYou are skilled in stealth and surviving far from the streets of a city, allowing you to scout ahead of your companions during expeditions. Rogues who embrace this archetype are at home in the wilderness and among barbarians and rangers, and many Scouts serve as the eyes and ears of war bands. Ambusher, spy, bounty hunter—these are just a few of the roles that Scouts assume as they range the world."},
  ["creature.scout.xmm2024"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 270\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two attacks, using Shortsword and Longbow in any combination.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 4, range 150/600 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.scout-captain.xmm2024"]={title="Scout Captain",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 270\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two attacks, using Shortsword or Longbow in any combination.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage, plus 10 (3d6) Piercing damage if the attack was made with XPHB.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 5, range 150/600 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, plus 10 (3d6) Piercing damage if the attack was made with XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAim\n\nThe scout has XPHB on the next attack roll it makes during the current turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nactTrigger The scout is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The scout halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.scrag.tftyp2014"]={title="Scrag",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 147\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30"},
  ["creature.scrapper.mismv12014"]={title="Scrapper",subtitle="Criatura - MisMV1 - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 126 (12d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: lightning\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nElectrified Chassis\n\nA creature that hits the scrapper with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 19 (3d12) lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scrapper makes two Spike Punch attacks. It can replace one of those with a Wires attack.\n\nSpike Punch\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 5 (1d10) piercing damage.\n\nWires\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one Large or smaller creature. hThe target has the grappled condition (escape 16) and must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be pulled into an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the scrapper and take 19 (3d12) lightning damage. The scrapper can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nEye Beam {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scrapper shoots a magical beam from its extended eye at one creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The target must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 44 (8d10) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.screaming-devilkin.mff2014"]={title="Screaming Devilkin",subtitle="Criatura - MFF - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAgile Flier\n\nOpportunity attacks against the screaming devilkin have disadvantage while it is flying.\n\nCeaseless Screaming\n\nAny creature other than a screaming devilkin that starts its turn within 30 feet of one or more screaming devilkins and can hear it must make a 10\n\nWisdom saving throw. On a failure the creature is incapacitated until the start of its next turn. On a success, the creature suffers no effect.\n\nStunted Legs\n\nThe screaming devilkin has disadvantage on attack rolls and all attack rolls made against it gain advantage while the devilkin isn't flying.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBarbed Tail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.scribble.crcotn2014"]={title="Scribble",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M"},
  ["background.scribe.xphb2024"]={title="Scribe",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 184\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.scribe-s-pen.erlw2014"]={title="Scribe's Pen",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 278\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can use this pen to write on any surface. You decide whether the writing is visible or invisible, but the writing is always visible to a person with the Mark of Scribing.\n\nAny creature with the Mark of Scribing can use an action to touch the invisible writing, making it visible to all.\n\nIf you use the pen to write on a creature that isn't a construct, the writing fades after 7 days."},
